{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceOnHecke","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeLiftInterface","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame_stabilizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame_stabilizes","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorReduction.lean#L164-L181","doc":"**Tower-stability of the observation frame, DERIVED from the Markov\nstabilization (bean `qou-ep0a`).** Given the general-`n` Markov stabilization\n`[MarkovStabilization …]` (the dependent conjecture in\n`HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold`), the observation frame is compatible with the\nHecke tower inclusion `ι`: `τ_∞(ι x) = τ_∞(x)`. This is the consequence that\nmakes `observationFrame` well-defined on the inductive-limit algebra — the\nstabilization feeds the derived frame. Sorry-free, derived (not assumed);\n`MarkovStabilization` still has no instance (general-`n` stays OPEN). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.tau_construction_reduces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.tau_construction_reduces","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorReduction.lean#L136-L162","doc":"**REDUCTION — constructing the observation side of τ reduces to two named\nopen items.** Threading the two existing, honestly-open conjecture classes as\nhypotheses:\n\n* `[MarkovTrace R H tr]` — the general-`n` Markov trace realizing\n  `tr_M = Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ` (open: only `n=2,3` are concrete; general `n` needs the\n  `Ind_{H_n}^{H_{n+1}}` stabilization);\n* `[TauRhoHodgeLift g W Wbar]` — τ carries the fibre reality ρ to Hodge\n  conjugation (open: THE wall, no instance anywhere),\n\nthis theorem DERIVES the exact two properties the α_EM per-loop measure\nderivation consumes:\n\n1. **gauge-invariance** of the observable (`τ_∞` cyclic), from the Markov trace;\n2. the **equal Hodge split** `Wbar.trace = W.trace` (the ½), from the lift.\n\nNeither is a class field — both are *derived* (§3b-cond rule 5, non-degenerate).\nSo \"construct the observation side of τ\" is reduced to exhibiting these two\ninstances (on top of the Hecke-category infrastructure F1/F2 that Lean cannot\nyet state). This DOES NOT discharge either hypothesis; the wall stands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.H3Concrete.obsH3_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.H3Concrete.obsH3_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorReduction.lean#L123-L130","doc":"**Concrete `n=3` gauge-invariance.** The observation frame on the full\n`H₃(q)` algebra product `mulNF` is cyclic — proved from the sorry-free\n`H3.trM_cyclic`. A genuine (non-vacuous) realization of the F3 slice at `n=3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.H3Concrete.obsH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.H3Concrete.obsH3","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorReduction.lean#L117-L121","doc":"The `n=3` observation frame `ev ∘ H3.trM` on the `Fin 6` NF module of\n`H₃(q)` (basis `[γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame_smul","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorReduction.lean#L94-L108","doc":"**Homogeneity of the observable, DERIVED.** From `MarkovTrace.map_smul` and\n`ev` a ring hom, `τ_∞(r • x) = ev(r) · τ_∞(x)` — the remaining third of the\n`R`-linearity a fibre-functor trace must respect (with the scalar carried\nacross the wall by `ev`). Together with `observationFrame_cyclic` /\n`observationFrame_add` this consumes ALL THREE `MarkovTrace` class fields —\nand nothing else: the W1 audit\n(`docs/audits/2026-07-25-markovtrace-w1-class-fields-audit.md`) confirms the\nconsumers need exactly cyclicity + linearity; Wenzl POSITIVITY is surplus to\nthe general-`n` instance gap (the #4151 PSD-surplus pattern), and is not even\nexpressible over the generic `[CommRing R]` this class lives on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame_add","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorReduction.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**Additivity of the observable, DERIVED.** From `MarkovTrace.map_add` and\n`ev` a ring hom, `τ_∞` is additive — part of the `R`-linearity a fibre-functor\ntrace must respect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorReduction.lean#L74-L82","doc":"**Gauge-invariance of the observable (part of F3), DERIVED.** Given a Markov\ntrace, the observation frame is cyclic: `τ_∞(xy) = τ_∞(yx)`. This is the\nnecessary condition for `τ_∞` to be a categorical trace — proved from\n`MarkovTrace.cyclic`, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauFunctorReduction.observationFrame","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauFunctorReduction.lean#L64-L72","doc":"**The observation frame `τ_∞`.** Modelling the two composable halves of the\nobservation side of τ: the Markov trace `tr : H → R` (the Frobenius pairing\n`tr_M`, pre-wall, generic `R`) followed by the archimedean evaluation\n`ev : R →+* ℝ` (the wall F4 — \"specialize `q` to the substrate `q₀`\", a ring\nhom). `τ_∞ = ev ∘ tr_M`. This is the *observation* half; the full τ additionally\ncarries the monoidal/braided structure (F1/F2) and the reality→Hodge lift (F5),\nnone of which this composition supplies. ","signatureChunk":0}]}